Dear Valued Customer, We hope this message finds you well. At SecureTech, your security and privacy are our top priorities. We are reaching out to inform you about some exciting updates we have implemented to enhance the security features of your account. Starting next week, we will be rolling out a two-factor authentication (2FA) option for all users. This additional layer of security will help protect your account from unauthorized access. Once enabled, you will be required to verify your identity through a secondary method—either via a text message or an authentication app—whenever you log in from an unrecognized device. To enable 2FA, simply follow these steps: 1. Log into your SecureTech account. 2. Navigate to the ""Account Settings"" section. 3. Click on ""Security"" and then select ""Enable Two-Factor Authentication."" 4. Follow the on-screen instructions to complete the setup. We also want to remind you of the importance of using strong, unique passwords for your accounts. If you haven’t changed your password in a while, we highly encourage you to do so. A strong password should be at least 12 characters long and include a mix of uppercase letters, lowercase letters, numbers, and special characters. Additionally, we are pleased to announce that we have improved our monitoring systems to detect any suspicious activity on your account. You will receive notifications for any unusual login attempts